#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:11
msgid "Exploring MPM materials and coupling"
msgstr "探索 MPM 材料与耦合"

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:13
msgid ""
"The Material Point Method (MPM) represents materials with particles that can"
" deform, compact, and flow. Stiffness, yielding, friction, and viscosity "
"determine how these materials respond to forces and collisions."
msgstr "物质点法（MPM）用粒子表示能够变形、压实和流动的材料。刚度、屈服、摩擦和黏度共同决定材料受力及碰撞时的响应。"

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:17
msgid ""
"In this tutorial, we compare material parameters in simple impact scenes, "
"explore the nearly rigid limit, and reconstruct a fluid surface from "
"particles. We then use a walking G1 robot to see how particle reaction "
"forces affect rigid-body motion. Each comparison helps isolate a different "
"part of the simulation so you can adapt the settings to your own scene."
msgstr ""
"本教程先在简单碰撞场景中对比材料参数，探索近似刚体的极限情况，并从粒子重建流体表面；随后让 G1 "
"机器人行走，观察粒子反作用力对刚体运动的影响。各组对比将仿真的不同因素分开考察，便于将这些设置用于自己的场景。"

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:23
msgid ""
"For an introduction to spawning MPM objects and configuring the Newton "
"solver, see :ref:`newton-using-mpm`. The comparisons below illustrate "
"qualitative behavior; they are starting points for experiments rather than "
"calibrated material models."
msgstr ""
"生成 MPM 对象和配置 Newton 求解器的入门说明见 :ref:`newton-using-mpm` "
"。下列对比用于展示定性行为，可作为实验起点，并非经过标定的材料模型。"

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:30
msgid "Running the tutorials"
msgstr "运行教程"

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:32
msgid ""
"The material and rigid-body tutorials launch Kit by default, requiring the "
"``isaacsim`` extra. The surface-reconstruction tutorial launches Newton GL "
"by default. Use ``--viz`` to select another visualizer; Newton RTX also "
"requires ``uv run --extra ovrtx``."
msgstr ""
"材料与刚体教程默认启动 Kit，需要安装 ``isaacsim`` 可选依赖。表面重建教程默认启动 Newton GL。可以用 ``--viz`` "
"选择其他可视化器；Newton RTX 还需要使用 ``uv run --extra ovrtx``。"

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:39
msgid "Comparing material parameters"
msgstr "对比材料参数"

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:41
msgid ""
"The ``material_parameters.py`` tutorial shows how one parameter changes a "
"material's response to impact. The stiffness and compressibility presets "
"drop spheres onto plates. The other presets drop blocks onto horizontal "
"cylinders, where you can observe spreading, fragmentation, and the shape "
"left after impact."
msgstr ""
"``material_parameters.py`` "
"教程展示单个参数如何改变材料的碰撞响应。刚度与可压缩性预设让球体落到平板上；其余预设让方块落到水平圆柱上，便于观察材料铺展、碎裂和碰撞后的形状。"

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:46
msgid "Elastic stiffness with ``--press_spheres``:"
msgstr "使用 ``--press_spheres`` 对比受压时的弹性刚度："

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:54
msgid "Start with the elastic stiffness comparison:"
msgstr "先从弹性刚度对比开始："

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:61
msgid ""
"The three specimens share the same geometry, initial velocities, particle "
"mass, solver settings, and seeded particle layout. Their Young's moduli are "
"100 kPa, 300 kPa, and 1 MPa. Compare how much each sphere compresses and how"
" it recovers after impact. Yielding is disabled in this preset to isolate "
"the elastic response."
msgstr ""
"三个试样采用相同的几何形状、初速度、粒子质量、求解器设置，以及由同一随机种子生成的粒子分布，杨氏模量分别为 100 kPa、300 kPa 和 1 "
"MPa。观察各球体的压缩程度和碰撞后的恢复过程。该预设关闭屈服，以单独考察弹性响应。"

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:67
msgid ""
"Each preset defines the varied field and the values that remain fixed. "
"``material_values_for_variant()`` combines these with the common material "
"settings before passing them to ``MPMParticleMaterialCfg``:"
msgstr ""
"每种预设都定义了变化的字段和保持不变的值。``material_values_for_variant()`` 将这些值与通用材料设置合并，再传给 "
"``MPMParticleMaterialCfg``："

#: source/how-to/mpm_tutorials.rst:75
msgid "Choose a preset according to the behavior you want to explore:"
msgstr "根据希望考察的行为选择预设："

